3
00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:22.592
<v NARRATOR>Rest is a heron-tween. She stands at the water's edge with one foot perpetually raised.

4
00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:31.923
<v NARRATOR>A small silver pocket-watch hangs from a chain around her neck. It is almost always silent.

5
00:00:31.923 --> 00:00:50.614
<v REST>I am Rest. The waiting is also the fishing. The waiting is my work.

6
00:00:50.614 --> 00:01:00.265
<v NARRATOR>Her pocket-watch ticks once, audibly, only when a meaningful pause is happening.

7
00:01:00.265 --> 00:01:15.876
<v REST>The pause *is* the action. In fishing. In conversation. In dialogue.

8
00:01:15.876 --> 00:01:35.087
<v REST>The silence speaks. It is a line of dialogue itself, but without words.

9
00:01:35.087 --> 00:01:40.978
<v NARRATOR>Patter met her at dawn. He saw her active stillness and he waited.

10
00:01:40.978 --> 00:01:50.989
<v REST>You waited. Most observers do not. They want the strike to come quickly.

11
00:01:50.989 --> 00:01:59.480
<v NARRATOR>In the workshop, Patter says a pause can be thoughtful, uncomfortable, or charged with meaning.

12
00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:18.571
<v REST>Without the pause, every line carries the same weight. With the pause, some lines land harder.

13
00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:24.942
<v REST>The pause is a line. The silence speaks. Use it.

14
00:02:24.942 --> 00:02:32.153
<v NARRATOR>One foot raised. A silver watch. She embodies the held pause.

15
00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:38.164
<v NARRATOR>The silence is not nothing. It is a line that does not have words.

16
